cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this MATLAB toolbox, please cite it using the 'preferred-citation' below. In addition, please cite the original scientific paper (Stockman & Rider, 2023) upon which this implementation is based."
title: "Individual Cone Fundamentals Toolbox (MATLAB)"
abstract: |
  Individual-observer cone fundamentals vary with opsin genotype, age, retinal field size, and the optical densities of the lens, macular pigment, and photopigment. We present a MATLAB toolbox that implements the Stockman and Rider formulae for generating individual cone spectral sensitivities from biophysical inputs. The toolbox uses a modular object-oriented design in which photopigment, lens, and macular templates can be independently selected or replaced. It computes LMS cone fundamentals, color matching functions, CIE XYZ tristimulus values, chromaticity coordinates, and photopic luminous efficiency functions from a single consistent observer parameterization. The implementation is validated against the reference Python implementation, pycone, across 28 observer configurations and five output formats, with residuals near expected double-precision numerical limits. The toolbox supports applications including age-dependent observer modeling, observer metamerism analysis, dichromacy simulation, and L/M opsin polymorphism studies. It is distributed as a MATLAB Add-On and is intended to support reproducible individual-observer colorimetry research.
